==Introduction==

===Abstract===

This document proposes a staged path for introducing zero-knowledge (ZK) proof support in transactions.
In the initial stage, a ZK proof commitment is embedded in a transaction output using a canonical OP_RETURN pattern, and the full proof bytes (public inputs and proof material) are published on-chain via a P2SH data-carrier reveal pattern (TX_C + TX_R), to enable immediate interoperability and chain-level observability without a consensus change.
In a later stage, this proposal is intended to migrate from OP_RETURN commitments to a dedicated reserved opcode path (for example via OP_SUCCESSx-based soft fork design, sometimes referred to as <code>OP_CHECKZKP</code>), enabling native script-level validation semantics and stronger on-chain composability.

The current implementation focus is Groth16 (snarkjs/rapidsnark-compatible JSON encoding), PLONK, and a placeholder for STARK_S2.
This document is written in standard BIP format and is a sibling proposal to the Post-Quantum Signature Commitments BIP, sharing the same TX_C + TX_R staging model and the same SPV scanning/log conventions.
It can be adapted to a DIP process if/when a formal DIP track is preferred.

